[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      3[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## How the axes were derived
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      4[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      5[0m:[38;5;10m[49m From `c_src/include/driver.h` and `c_src/src/driver.c` only.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      6[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      7[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Public entry points (from the header).** Exactly one:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      8[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      9[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```c
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     10[0m:[38;5;10m[49m void driver(double f);
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     11[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     12[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     13[0m:[38;5;10m[49m There is no init/teardown, no context object, no setter, no lower-level variant,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m and no convenience wrapper — so "exercise the low-level entry points, not just
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m the wrappers" collapses to: `driver` *is* the low-level entry point, and it is
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m the only symbol the `.so` exports (see `SYMBOLS.md`). The three units the C
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m composes internally are the three conversions of the single `printf` call, and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m the only way to reach them is through `driver`. The Rust helpers
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m (`format_llx`, `format_hex_double`, `format_fixed_4`, `render`, `write_stdout`)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m are private and deliberately **not** called directly by the tests — everything
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m goes through the `.so` export.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Runtime options / modes / flags.** None. `grep` for `if` / `switch` / `#if` in
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m the code region returns 0 hits (see `ERRORS.md`), and the function takes no flag
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m parameter. So the configuration surface is *entirely* the shape of the single
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `double` argument, plus the two ambient process settings glibc's conversions
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m genuinely branch on.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Axes the C actually distinguishes** (all branching lives in the glibc
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m conversions the C selects with its format string `"%llx %a %.4f\n"`):
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | axis | values the code treats differently |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     33[0m:[38;5;10m[49m |------|------------------------------------|
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     34[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `sign` | sign bit clear / set (affects `%llx` digit count, `%a` leading `-`, `%.4f` leading `-` — including on zero and NaN) |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     35[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `expfield` | `0` (zero + subnormal: `%a` leading digit `0`, exponent pinned to `-1022`) · `1` (first normal, also `p-1022`) · `2..0x3fe` (`p-` exponents) · `0x3ff` (`p+0`) · `0x400..0x7fd` (`p+` exponents) · `0x7fe` (`p+1023`, max normal, must not be read as inf) · `0x7ff` (inf when mantissa 0, NaN otherwise) |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     36[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `mantissa` | `0` (`%a` emits **no** radix point) · trailing zero nibbles (trimmed) · low nibble set (all 13 digits kept) · all ones · arbitrary |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     37[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `llx width` | 1 … 16 significant hex digits; no padding, no leading zeroes; `0` prints as `0` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     38[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `%.4f` magnitude | `0` · `(0, 5e-5)` → `0.0000` · `[5e-5, 1)` · `[1, 1e4)` · `[1e4, 1e15)` · `[1e15, 1e17)` (fraction always exactly `.0000`) · `[1e100, 1e200)` · `[1e300, DBL_MAX]` (309 integer digits) |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     39[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `%.4f` rounding | below the 4-digit boundary · above it · exactly-representable tie with **even** 4th digit · exactly-representable tie with **odd** 4th digit · carry propagation into the integer part |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     40[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | stream state | fresh buffer vs. mid-line buffered `FILE*` across repeated calls |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     41[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | ambient (not settable through `driver.h`) | `LC_NUMERIC` decimal point; FP rounding mode — glibc's `%a`/`%.4f` read both |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     42[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     43[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Rows below are the pruned cross-product: one row per combination the C treats
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     44[0m:[38;5;10m[49m differently. **Every row is exercised with many randomized inputs from a fixed
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     45[0m:[38;5;10m[49m seed** (`SEED = 0x5EED_D1FF_2025`, splitmix64), not a single hand-picked value;
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     46[0m:[38;5;10m[49m the fixed special values that define a row's boundary are included in that row's
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     47[0m:[38;5;10m[49m input set. Total values compared: see the test output summary.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     48[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
