[0m[49m[39m   93,  93[0m:[39m[49m They are listed because glibc's conversions *do* branch on them, so a caller
[0m[49m[38;5;9m-  94     [0m:[38;5;9m[49m that changes them can observe a difference. The tests set them explicitly and
[0m[49m[38;5;9m-  95     [0m:[38;5;9m[49m compare C against Rust; see the test report for the outcome and for which of
